From: Duron27 <duron27@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] A server takes 128 players and tells the rest it is full

- relay: hard cap of 128 players whatever --max-players says (a hosting game counts as one of them); parties stay at 3
- components/net: more sockets than players (192), so connections beyond the cap get a join_result 'full' instead of being
  cut off
- mpserver --help: at most 128
- capacity_test.py starts the real server and joins 135 players; relay tests for the clamp and the party limit

---
